 is divisible by $2$, **then** $10$ is divisible by $5.$\n- **If** $9$ is divisible by $5$, **then** $6$ is divisible by $3.$" :question/worked-solution "An implication $A⇒B$ is true *unless* $A$ is true and $B$ is false. In other words, the implication is true unless the \"promise\" is broken.\n\n- Statement I is false. The antecedent \"$12$ is divisible by $3$\" is true, and the consequent \"$9$ is divisible by $4$\" is false. So the promise is broken, and the statement is false.\n\n- Statement II is true. The antecedent \"$5$ is divisible by $2$\" is false, so the promise does not apply. Regardless of the consequent, the promise is *not* broken, and the statement is true.\n\n- Statement III is true. Again, the antecedent \"$9$ is divisible by $5$\" is false, so the promise does not apply. Regardless of the consequent, the promise is *not* broken, and the statement is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406982 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059706 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1e1c01fd-dea0-5761-9499-d622a34fea3e" :knowledge-point/title "Completing a Truth Table With Compound Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a334099-1f7f-5c0b-aead-371217a694de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{F}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406966} {:answer/id #uuid "a2888028-3901-5c34-ae8a-4a28ac3aca86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{T}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406969}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2888028-3901-5c34-ae8a-4a28ac3aca86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{T}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406969} :answer-field/id #uuid "2aee77f4-9be5-5c3a-80a1-10941ff43d8b" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select