/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{F}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406971}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d6a50a3-bb24-530f-a62b-129c6bdb591b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{T}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406961} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4032492-1493-553b-bc31-fe628a9c1050" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406979}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e0bd03cd-0c48-596c-b039-0f9c85a18c3a" :question/math-academy-id "q-182663" :question/problem "Find the missing values in the following truth table:" :question/worked-solution "First, we add columns for $¬P,$ $¬Q$ and $¬P∨¬Q:$\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,¬P\\,$ | $\\,¬Q\\,$ | $\\,¬P∨¬Q\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nNow, we add a column for $P⇒(¬P∨¬Q).$ This statement is true unless $P$ is true and $¬P∨¬Q$ is false. \n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,¬P\\,$ | $\\,¬Q\\,$ | $\\,¬P∨¬Q\\,$ | $\\,P⇒(¬P∨¬Q)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406981 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059707 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "64a3922f-7e74-562f-9bb9-c4a41e912ce7" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Conditional Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c24a347-5951-5876-9f2d-8a1d7c5b9f75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406956} {:answer/id #uuid "383d59b8-a864-5389-8975-dc9bbacfa5e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406957} {:answer/id #uuid "5017cc1a-c69b-5371-9aff-5e273c1bbfe5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406959} {:answer/id #uuid "9ca16a39-9404-5469-a817-d4f31a93d630" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406968} {:answer/id #uuid "ac3fcded-1928-518d-b875-ec2601c5af9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406970}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "383d59b8-a864-5389-8975-dc9bbacfa5e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406957} :answer-field/id #uuid "1cad3447-1622-501b-827e-837284b22076" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406974}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "806aafe6-aa9d-53f3-a7d9-19809d388a29" :question/math-academy-id "q-82092" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- **If** $7$ is an even number, **then** $6$ is an odd number.\n- **If** $6$ is an even number, **then** $7$ is an even number.\n- **If** $6$ is an even number, **then** $7$ is an odd number." :question/worked-solution "An implication $A⇒B$ is true *unless* $A$ is true and $B$ is false. In other words, the implication is true unless the \"promise\" is broken.\n\n- Statement I is true. The antecedent \"$7$ is an even number\" is false, so the promise does not apply. Regardless of the consequent, the promise is *not* broken, and the statement is true.\n\n- Statement II is false. The antecedent \"$6$ is an even number\" is true, and the consequent \"$7$ is an even number\" is false. So the promise is broken, and the statement is false.\n\n- Statement III is true. The antecedent \"$6$ is an even number\" is true, and the consequent \"$7$ is an odd number\" is true. So the promise is kept, and the statement is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}]}
